"""Native straight or two-circle continuation between nearly opposing curbs.

Contacts use equal outward chord stations on the original certified paths.
The two circles turn in opposite directions and retain the requested radius.
Sampled brackets seed bisection; distinct admissible roots remain explicit.
This primitive does not certify a complete perimeter or pavement footprint.
Original-port kind 3 denotes a zero-length join at a shared whole-Street knot.
Its two original curb pieces are evaluated by the enclosing chart, not here.
"""
